---
import ImageSlot from './ImageSlot.astro';
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import { stats } from '../data/site';
---

<section class="section opp" id="opportunity" aria-labelledby="opp-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="grid opp__head">
      <div class="opp__side">
        <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>The executive opportunity</p>
        <ImageSlot
          label="Leaders reviewing AI results"
          src="/images/leaders-reviewing.jpg"
          alt="Leaders reviewing results together at a meeting table"
          ratio="4 / 5"
          tone="stone"
          class="opp__img"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="opp__intro">
        <h2 class="h2" id="opp-title" data-split>From AI Activity to <em>Business Value</em></h2>
        <p class="lede opp__lede" data-reveal style="--i:1">
          AI activity is expanding across organizations. The executive opportunity is to translate individual
          gains and promising use cases into measurable business performance.
        </p>

        <p class="opp__kicker" data-reveal>
          <span class="chip"><Icon name="book-open-text" /> McKinsey, The State of AI in 2026</span>
          <span>McKinsey's 2026 global survey found:</span>
        </p>

        <ul class="opp__stats" role="list">
          {stats.map((s, i) => (
            <li class="stat" data-reveal style={`--i:${i}`}>
              <p class="stat__value" aria-label={s.label ?? s.value}>
                {s.prefix && <span class="stat__prefix">{s.prefix}</span>}
                {s.value.endsWith('%') ? (
                  <span data-count={parseInt(s.value)} data-suffix="%">{s.value}</span>
                ) : (
                  <span>{s.value}</span>
                )}
              </p>
              <span class="stat__bar" style={`--w:${s.value.endsWith('%') ? parseInt(s.value) : 74}%`}></span>
              <p class="stat__text">{s.text}</p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>

        <p class="cite opp__cite" data-reveal>
          McKinsey, The State of AI in 2026: On the Road to ROI, August 2026. 1,719 participants in 97 countries,
          surveyed May 4 to June 8, 2026. AI high performers are a small subgroup of 92 respondents, and the workflow
          finding is an association within that group. The profit measure is earnings before interest and taxes; the
          productivity and profit percentages describe different outcomes.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid opp__close">
      <span class="opp__quote-icon" data-reveal><Icon name="quotes" /></span>
      <p class="opp__question" data-reveal>
        For leaders, the value question extends beyond the technology: which business priorities merit
        investment, how should the work and workflow change, and what operating conditions will help the new
        way of working produce measurable results?
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .opp__head {
    row-gap: 48px;
  }
  .opp__side {
    grid-column: 1 / 5;
    padding-top: 14px;
  }
  .opp__side :global(.opp__img) {
    margin-top: 40px;
    position: sticky;
    top: 120px;
  }
  .opp__intro {
    grid-column: 6 / 13;
  }
  .opp__lede {
    margin-top: 28px;
  }
  .opp__kicker {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-top: clamp(56px, 7vw, 88px);
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  .opp__stats {
    list-style: none;
    margin-top: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
  }
  .stat {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 6fr);
    column-gap: 32px;
    align-items: end;
    padding: 32px 0 28px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .stat__value {
    grid-row: span 2;
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 12px;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(64px, 7.4vw, 108px);
    line-height: 0.92;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 72;
  }
  .stat__prefix {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--teal);
  }
  .stat__bar {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    height: 2px;
    background: var(--line);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .stat__bar::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: var(--w);
    background: var(--teal);
    transform: scaleX(0);
    transform-origin: left;
    transition: transform 1.6s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1) 0.2s;
  }
  .stat.is-in .stat__bar::after,
  :global(html:not(.js)) .stat__bar::after {
    transform: none;
  }
  .stat__text {
    margin-top: 16px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .opp__cite {
    margin-top: 28px;
  }
  .opp__close {
    margin-top: clamp(80px, 10vw, 136px);
    row-gap: 16px;
  }
  .opp__quote-icon {
    grid-column: 4 / 5;
    justify-self: end;
    color: var(--teal);
  }
  .opp__quote-icon :global(.icon) {
    width: 44px;
    height: 44px;
  }
  .opp__question {
    grid-column: 5 / 12;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(22px, 2.1vw, 30px);
    line-height: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: -0.008em;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  @media (max-width: 899px) {
    .opp__side :global(.opp__img) {
      position: relative;
      top: auto;
      max-width: 360px;
    }
    .opp__quote-icon {
      justify-self: start;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 599px) {
    .stat {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .stat__value {
      grid-row: auto;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }
  }
</style>
